I stumbled upon https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/108993 which changes how we compute inhabitedness. If I follow correctly, this would mean we don't look into inferred types to determine inhabitedness. So the following, which works today ([play](https://play.rust-lang.org/?version=nightly&mode=debug&edition=2021&gist=7f4138007cfecd2ab4f3f0a7313da32c)), would error instead:
```rust
#![feature(min_exhaustive_patterns)]
#![allow(unused)]

fn infer<F: FnOnce() -> R, R>(_: Result<bool, R>) {}

enum Void {}
fn with_void() {
    let mut x = Ok(true);
    match x {
        Ok(_) => {}
    }
    infer::<fn() -> Void, _>(x)
}
```

Hence https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/108993 becomes a breaking change. We thus need to decide whether to accept https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/108993 before we stabilize `min_exhaustive_patterns`.

